  "problem_statement": "*** Problem Statement ***\n\nDimensions of Borel Orbits on Matrix Spaces over $\\mathbb{C}$\nLet $X = M(m,n)$ be the vector space of $m \\times n$ real matrices. Let $B_m \\subset GL_m(\\mathbb{C})$ and $B_n \\subset GL_n(\\mathbb{C})$ be the Borel subgroups consisting of upper triangular matrices. \n\nA **partial matching** $pm$ is a subset of the product set $[m] \\times [n]$ such that for any two distinct pairs $(i, j), (i', j') \\in pm$, we have $i \\neq i'$ and $j \\neq j'$. \nFor each $pm$, we define a representative matrix $A_{pm} \\in X$ where:\n$$(A_{pm})_{ij} = \\begin{cases} 1 & \\text{if } (i, j) \\in pm \\\\ 0 & \\text{otherwise} \\end{cases}$$\n\nConsider the action of the Lie group $G = B_m \\times B_n$ on $X$ defined by:\n$$\\Phi: (B_m \\times B_n) \\times X \\to X, \\quad (b_1, b_2) \\cdot A = b_1 A b_2^{T}$$\nHere $b_2^T$ is the transpose of the matrix $b_2$. \nLet $Y_{pm}$ denote the orbit $G \\cdot A_{pm}$.\n\nGoal: Compute the dimension of the orbit $Y_{pm}$. \n\nHint: The dimension of $Y_{pm} = dim B_1 + dim B_2 -  dim Stab_{B_1 \\times B_2}(A_pm)$. \nTo compute $dim Stab_{B_1 \\times B_2}(A_pm)$ one can reduce the problem to compute the dimension of its Lie algebra. \n\n\n",
